  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 215 AM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nSaturday-Sunday:\nCooler and dry weather persist into the weekend. As high\npressure settles overhead, highs remain in the 50s to near 60 on\nSaturday afternoon. Another cold night into Sunday morning, with\nareas of frost and freeze likely again. Additional headlines\nwill be assessed as needed, as we come to the end of the \ngrowing season.\n\nA touch warmer into Sunday with seasonable highs back into the\nmiddle 60s. This will mark the beginning of a warming trend\ninto next week.\n\nNext Week:\nA ridge overspreads the central CONUS into next week, with\nincreasing mid-level heights supporting a warming trend.\nConfidence is high in temperatures 5 to 10 degrees above \nnormal, with daily highs in the upper 60s to around 70. \nOvernight lows in the upper 30s to middle 40s. There is some \nuncertainty in the extent of the mild temperatures late in the \nweek, as ensemble guidance begin to diverge.",
